From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick DiZazzo <nick.dizazzo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:37:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] test(skippy): reproduce #2158 temperature-0 chains skip
 the argmax path

A temperature-0 request with ignore_eos, a logit bias, or penalties
whose window is zero cannot select anything but the top biased logit,
yet it is not treated as greedy. Every decoded row copies the whole
vocabulary and runs the full sampler chain on the scheduler thread.

Add an argmax mode to skippy-sampling-history. It decodes such requests
with the sampler order and defaults the serving layer sends and checks
that every token equals the token a freshly built full chain selects.
It also checks that every row took the argmax path, counted by a new
session counter, and that equal biased maxima fall back to the full
chain.
